.TH FL-PRINTERS 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-printers \- printer settings for fldesktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-printers\fR [\fB\-\-add\fR] [\fIPRINTER\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists the printers of the CUPS printing service and their jobs. A printer can
be added (found printers are offered; network printers are set up
driverless with IPP Everywhere, others with a matching driver), removed,
made the default, paused, set to accept or reject jobs, shared, renamed and
given a location. Its default paper size, two-sided and color settings can
be changed, and a test page printed. Jobs can be canceled.
.PP
The same view is the Printers page of \fBfl-settings\fR(1). While documents
are printing, \fBfl-panel\fR(1) shows a printer button with the queue, and a
notification tells when a document has been printed or could not be.
.PP
Changing printers needs administrator rights in CUPS (membership of the
lpadmin or sys group, or root); otherwise fl-printers asks for a password.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-add\fR
Open the Add Printer dialog right away.
.TP
\fIPRINTER\fR
Select this printer (queue name).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBCUPS_SERVER\fR
The CUPS server to use (default: the local scheduler).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBlpadmin\fR(8), \fBlpstat\fR(1), \fBcupsd\fR(8), \fBfl-settings\fR(1)
